# The tour's reads over HTTP.
# 1. Start the API:  dotnet run --project Zooper.Ant.Example -- --serve
# 2. Send the requests in order from Visual Studio, Rider or VS Code (REST Client). Requests marked `# @name` remember
#    their response, so later requests pick up the token themselves; there is nothing to copy.

@host = http://localhost:5080

### 1. First continuable page (the default kind): 3 players and a nextPageToken
# @name page1
GET {{host}}/players?size=3

### 2. The next page: send the token back
GET {{host}}/players?size=3&pageToken={{page1.response.body.$.nextPageToken}}

### 3. The size may change between pages...
GET {{host}}/players?size=5&pageToken={{page1.response.body.$.nextPageToken}}

### 4. ...the filters may not: the same token for team=blue is refused (400 "Invalid page token")
GET {{host}}/players?size=3&team=blue&pageToken={{page1.response.body.$.nextPageToken}}

### 5. Counted: page 2 of size 3, with the total count
GET {{host}}/players?paging=counted&page=2&size=3

### 6. Counted deeper than the limit of 30 rows: refused (400)
GET {{host}}/players?paging=counted&page=11&size=3

### 7. Capped: the top 3 of team red, and whether more matched
GET {{host}}/players?paging=capped&cap=3&team=red

### 8. An argument of another kind is refused, not ignored (400)
GET {{host}}/players?paging=capped&cap=3&page=2

### 9. A size above the maximum of 10 is clamped and served
GET {{host}}/players?size=500

### 10. Another order, reversed: Name descending
GET {{host}}/players?sort=Name&reverse=true&size=4

### 11. A filter that cannot match: an empty counted page, nothing read
GET {{host}}/players?paging=counted&minRating=101

### 12. Live data: add a player, then repeat request 2; Zoe (85) now appears on page 2
POST {{host}}/players
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zoe", "team": "red", "rating": 85 }

### 13. Everyone, streamed by following the tokens
GET {{host}}/players/export

### 14. A store with its own cursors: continuable works
GET {{host}}/activity?size=3

### 15. ...counted does not: the store cannot count (400)
GET {{host}}/activity?paging=counted

### 16. The OpenAPI document: /players answers oneOf the three page shapes, paging lists its three values
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
